    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30440" root="علو" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُعْتَلٍ</span></b>  (assumed tropical:)  <i>Having ability,</i> or <i>power;</i> as also
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُسْتَعْلٍ</span></b> . (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [Hence,] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">المُعْتَلِى</span> signifies
(assumed tropical:)  <i>The lion;</i> (K, TA;) because of his strength.
(TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَلِىٌّ</span>, last quarter. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُوَ غَيْرُ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُعْتَلٍ فِى الأَمْرِ</span> means <i>He is not one who falls
short,</i> or <i>falls short of doing what is requisite,</i> or
<i>who is remiss, in the affair;</i> like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَيْرُ مُؤْتَلٍ</span>.
(TA.)

